# Isolated Presidio env (C4 / SPEC §11 heavy-ML-closure principle): presidio's
# spaCy + en_core_web_lg NER-model closure is the heavy-scientific-Python class
# the platform lock (uv.lock) MUST NOT carry (C4 license-gate false-positive
# exposure + sovereign-deploy bloat). It is confined here
# (packages/ne-govern/.presidio-venv) and NEVER enters the platform lock/SBOM.
# Same isolation pattern as packages/ne-brain/parser_env (docling). Compile with:
#
#   uv pip compile packages/ne-govern/presidio_env/requirements.in \
#       --universal --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes \
#       --override packages/ne-govern/presidio_env/overrides.txt \
#       -o packages/ne-govern/presidio_env/requirements.txt
#
# overrides.txt exists to lift presidio-anonymizer 2.2.363's stale cryptography<47
# ceiling so the compile takes the GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf fix (>=48.0.1); see
# overrides.txt for the full rationale and the unpin trigger.
#
# NEVER hand-edit requirements.txt.
presidio-analyzer==2.2.363
presidio-anonymizer==2.2.363
